        },
        "Text": {
          "type": "cexolocstring",
          "value": {
            "0": "*He jerks a thumb at the meadow and the great rock beyond* Three hives: one in the garden here, two on the Carrock -- the lesser height and the greater. The honey is yours to cut; the bees will forgive you by winter. But every broken hive sings to the wargs like a dinner-horn, so the killing and the harvesting are one job, not two. Six pelts, three combs, and gold from the stores when it is done."
          }
        }
      },
      {
